WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.960
CBS ran the iconic yet occasionally controversial&nbsp;
"Big Bang Theory" from September 2007&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.440
to the show's conclusion in May 2019. Instead of&nbsp;
focusing on families or co-workers, the series put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:20.080
the spotlight on folks that rarely get a say in&nbsp;
most big-budget productions: nerds. In doing so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.920
"Big Bang" made it cool to be a geek and embrace&nbsp;
whatever aspects of science, pop culture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.920
and general entertainment spoke to you via&nbsp;
an ensemble cast of unforgettable characters.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.800
One of those aforementioned&nbsp;
nerds was Howard Wolowitz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.920
the horniest and creepiest of the bright friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.960
While he often made inappropriate advances toward&nbsp;
the females around him, he did eventually find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.240
love. He settled down with an addition to the&nbsp;
cast named Bernadette, played by Melissa Rauch.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.760
Throughout many seasons, we got to know Bernadette&nbsp;
quite well. As we saw time and time again on "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:59.120
Big Bang Theory," Bernadette was a good friend,&nbsp;
spouse, scientist, and mother. However, there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:05.360
one major negative element about her personality&nbsp;
that was never shy about rearing its ugly head.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.560
At her core, Bernadette was a mild-mannered,&nbsp;
kind woman who wanted to see those around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.640
her live their best lives just as&nbsp;
much as she wanted to do so herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.280
She didn't always display these attributes,&nbsp;
though, especially when she found herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.160
in competitive situations, no matter&nbsp;
how inconsequential. She'd transform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:29.840
into a determined and unapologetically&nbsp;
harsh person — often slinging insults&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:35.680
left and right regardless as to who was around&nbsp;
her. Even Howard wasn't immune to her wrath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.960
finding himself on the receiving end of his wife's&nbsp;
rage more times than he surely wanted to be.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:46.080
Despite all of this, Bernadette's short fuse&nbsp;
didn't always end up putting just her friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.600
in her crosshairs. She could also use her fiery&nbsp;
spirit in such a way that would actually protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:57.520
the people she cares about, driving off anyone who&nbsp;
unjustly dared disrespect them in front of her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:03.120
She shows no hesitation when standing up for&nbsp;
Howard and even defends Stuart from a rival&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:08.560
comic book store owner's bullying. Given her&nbsp;
presentation as a quiet, easy-going young lady,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.960
they never see it coming, hence the&nbsp;
hilarity of these particular scenes.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:18.480
When provoked, Bernadette could become a&nbsp;
terrifying person that didn't discriminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.080
when it came to verbally attacking&nbsp;
other people. This is obviously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.640
not the best character trait to have, but&nbsp;
it's aided by the fact that she tends to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.040
use it in defense of the ones she loves&nbsp;
more often than not. It only ever really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.960
became a problem when her loved ones&nbsp;
were on the wrong side of her scorn.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.400
A feisty attitude is one thing. It's another thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.280
entirely to become obsessive to the point&nbsp;
where you demean the person you love most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.840
in the world. And that was something&nbsp;
Bernadette was not afraid of doing.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.200
If there were a single episode that best&nbsp;
encapsulated Bernadette's competitive nature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.960
it would be Season 12, Episode 9, "The Citation&nbsp;
Negation." This episode sees Howard and Raj&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.680
becoming obsessed with the video game sensation&nbsp;
"Fortnite." Bernadette wants to get in on the fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.640
but there's just one problem — she's not&nbsp;
very good at the game. She enlists the help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.840
of Denise to teach her the ways of "Fortnite,"&nbsp;
but no matter how much she practices, she still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.000
can't get better than her husband. When&nbsp;
Howard kills Bernadette's character quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.120
she responds with an obviously embarrassed jab.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:21.920
"Howard?"

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:22.480
"What?"

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.600
"I make more money than you!"

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.320
The funny thing is that Howard never made fun&nbsp;
of her for being bad at "Fortnite" He also had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:34.400
no problem letting her play for a little bit&nbsp;
to see what the game was like for herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.480
How nice. Her competitive side&nbsp;
wouldn't allow Howard and Raj&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:43.200
to have a fun activity for the two of them&nbsp;
to share. She had to become the best at it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:49.440
and when she failed, she had to find another way&nbsp;
to demonstrate her superiority over her husband.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.080
Granted, we're probably looking too deeply&nbsp;
into this personality trait. We know it's all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:59.600
meant for laughs. However, regardless of how you&nbsp;
feel about Bernadette, you have to admit Melissa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:05.200
Rauch's performance is second-to-none, even if&nbsp;
it made the character a bit unlikeable at times.

